<p>A <code>Document</code> draws no text until a font is registered with it — <code>addFont()</code> and <code>addFonts()</code> register a
standard PDF font; a font file goes through <code>embedFont()</code> instead, covered on <a href="/build/embedded-fonts">Embedding
Fonts</a>. Fonts live with the <code>Document</code> itself, not on any one <code>Page</code> — register
a font once and every page that references it by name draws with it.</p>
<h2 id="adding-a-font">Adding a Font<a class="anchor" href="#adding-a-font" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>addFont()</code> takes either a standard font name or a <code>Document\Font</code> instance, and <code>addFonts()</code> takes an
array of either:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Font</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>));
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFonts</span>([<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">HELVETICA</span>, <span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">TIMES_BOLD</span>]);

<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getAvailableFonts</span>(); <span class="text-comment">// [&#039;Helvetica&#039;, &#039;Times-Bold&#039;]</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>A bare string is wrapped in <code>new Font($name)</code> for you, so <code>addFont(Font::HELVETICA)</code> and
<code>addFont(new Font(Font::HELVETICA))</code> register the same thing. Registering the same name twice is a
no-op — the original <code>Font</code> instance is kept, and a distinct object built separately for that name is
discarded:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-var">$first</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Font</span>(<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">HELVETICA</span>);
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFont</span>(<span class="text-var">$first</span>);
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFont</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Font</span>(<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">HELVETICA</span>)); <span class="text-comment">// discarded, &#039;Helvetica&#039; is already registered</span>

<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getFont</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Helvetica&#039;</span>) <span class="text-kw">===</span> <span class="text-var">$first</span>; <span class="text-comment">// true — the original instance, untouched</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Safe to repeat across a codebase without checking <code>isFontAvailable()</code> first. Each successful
registration also becomes the document's current font — see <a href="#selecting-the-current-font">Selecting the Current
Font</a>.</p>
<p><code>addFont()</code> also accepts a path to a font file in place of a standard name, and hands it straight to
<code>embedFont()</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFont</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/fonts/DejaVuSans.ttf&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getAvailableFonts</span>(); <span class="text-comment">// [&#039;DejaVuSans&#039;]</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><a href="/build/embedded-fonts">Embedding Fonts</a> covers that path in full — formats, Unicode and glyph coverage.
Everything below concerns the standard fonts, which never touch a file.</p>
