<h3 id="the-benefits-of-standard-fonts">The Benefits of Standard Fonts<a class="anchor" href="#the-benefits-of-standard-fonts" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<ul>
<li>A standard font is referenced by name only</li>
<li>Render text from a common set of fonts without having to reach for and mange font files</li>
<li>Nothing goes into the PDF beyond a <code>/BaseFont</code> entry naming it — no heavy font file travels with it</li>
<li>This can help keep the filesize very low</li>
</ul>
<p>No font file has to be present at build time either — each name backs a class in
<code>Build\Font\Standard\</code> with its own glyph widths, so <code>new Font(Font::HELVETICA)</code> works with nothing
installed. The tradeoff: a standard name always builds and costs the document nothing, but draws in
whatever the reader's viewer supplies for that name — see <a href="/build/embedded-fonts">Embedding Fonts</a>.</p>
<p><code>Font::standardFonts()</code> and the instance method <code>getStandardFonts()</code> return the same array — the
static form needs no <code>Font</code> object in hand, and it's what backs the table above.</p>
<h3 id="how-a-standard-font-draws-text">How a Standard Font Draws Text<a class="anchor" href="#how-a-standard-font-draws-text" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p>A standard font's content stream carries WinAnsiEncoding (Windows-1252) bytes, one byte per
character, not the UTF-8 bytes a PHP string arrives in. <code>café</code> set in <code>Font::ARIAL</code> reaches the page as
the four bytes <code>63 61 66 E9</code> — not UTF-8's two-byte <code>C3 A9</code> for é — and <code>Pdf::extractTextFromFile()</code>
reads it straight back as <code>café</code>, since the encoding round trips both ways:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Text</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Font</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>));
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFont</span>(<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">ARIAL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPage</span>(<span class="text-num">1</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addText</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Text</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;café&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">size</span>: <span class="text-num">24</span>), <span class="text-str">&#039;Arial&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">72</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">700</span>);

<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-var">$document</span>, <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/winansi.pdf&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/winansi.pdf&#039;</span>); <span class="text-comment">// &#039;café&#039;</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>WinAnsiEncoding covers Latin-1 but not every script — a character the font's glyph table has no entry
for stops the document at compile time, rather than reaching the page as a missing or substitute
glyph:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPage</span>(<span class="text-num">1</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addText</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Text</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;中&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">size</span>: <span class="text-num">24</span>), <span class="text-str">&#039;Arial&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">72</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">730</span>);

<span class="text-kw">try</span> {
    <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-var">$document</span>, <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/fail.pdf&#039;</span>);
} <span class="text-kw">catch</span> (<span class="text-type">\Pop\Pdf\Build\Font\Exception</span> <span class="text-var">$exception</span>) {
    <span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$exception</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getMessage</span>();
    <span class="text-comment">// Error: The font &#039;Arial&#039; does not contain a glyph for character &#039;中&#039; (U+4E2D).</span>
}
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>This is the same <code>hasGlyph()</code>/<code>requireGlyphCoverage()</code> machinery <a href="/build/embedded-fonts#glyph-coverage">Embedding
Fonts</a> covers for embedded fonts — a standard <code>Font</code> answers
both, checked against its own built-in glyph table rather than a parsed file's cmap.</p>
<h2 id="selecting-the-current-font">Selecting the Current Font<a class="anchor" href="#selecting-the-current-font" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>getCurrentFont()</code> reports whichever font was most recently registered, and <code>setCurrentFont()</code> moves
that pointer to a font already on the document:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Font</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>();
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFonts</span>([<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">HELVETICA</span>, <span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">TIMES_BOLD</span>]);
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getCurrentFont</span>(); <span class="text-comment">// &#039;Times-Bold&#039; — the last one added</span>

<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setCurrentFont</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Helvetica&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getCurrentFont</span>(); <span class="text-comment">// &#039;Helvetica&#039;</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Naming a font that has not been registered raises <code>Document\Exception</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">try</span> {
    <span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setCurrentFont</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Arial&#039;</span>); <span class="text-comment">// never registered on $document</span>
} <span class="text-kw">catch</span> (<span class="text-type">\Pop\Pdf\Document\Exception</span> <span class="text-var">$exception</span>) {
    <span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$exception</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getMessage</span>();
    <span class="text-comment">// Error: The font &#039;Arial&#039; has not been added to the PDF document.</span>
}
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>A document with no fonts registered answers <code>getCurrentFont()</code> with <code>null</code>, not a fallback name.</p>
<p>Neither method changes what <code>addText()</code> draws with — every call still takes its own <code>$fontStyle</code>,
with no implicit fallback to the current font. <code>getCurrentFont()</code> exists to avoid a repeated literal:
register once, then pass <code>$document-&gt;getCurrentFont()</code> into <code>addText()</code> instead of retyping the name.</p>
<h2 id="measuring-a-string">Measuring a String<a class="anchor" href="#measuring-a-string" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>getStringWidth($string, $size)</code> reports how wide a string renders in a <code>Font</code>, in points, at the given
size — call it on the <code>Font</code> object a document already holds, not on the constant:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Font</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>));
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFont</span>(<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">HELVETICA</span>);
<span class="text-var">$font</span> = <span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getFont</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Helvetica&#039;</span>);

<span class="text-var">$font</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getStringWidth</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Centered Heading&#039;</span>, <span class="text-num">24</span>); <span class="text-comment">// 194.76</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Width scales linearly with size — the same string measures 97.38 points at 12pt and 389.52 at 48pt,
each exactly double the size before it. A width measured once can be scaled rather than remeasured,
though remeasuring at the real size costs about the same and never drifts out of sync.</p>
<p>Centering that heading on a 612-point letter page is a matter of subtracting the measured width from
the page width and halving what's left:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Text</span>;

<span class="text-var">$width</span> = <span class="text-var">$font</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getStringWidth</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Centered Heading&#039;</span>, <span class="text-num">24</span>);
<span class="text-var">$x</span>     = (<span class="text-num">612</span> - <span class="text-var">$width</span>) / <span class="text-num">2</span>; <span class="text-comment">// 208.62</span>

<span class="text-var">$page</span> = <span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPage</span>(<span class="text-num">1</span>);
<span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addText</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Text</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Centered Heading&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">size</span>: <span class="text-num">24</span>), <span class="text-str">&#039;Helvetica&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-var">$x</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">700</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The same measurement fits a string to a box by shrinking the size until it stops overflowing, rather
than by picking a size and hoping:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-var">$string</span>   = <span class="text-str">&#039;Quarterly Revenue Summary&#039;</span>;
<span class="text-var">$maxWidth</span> = <span class="text-num">200</span>;
<span class="text-var">$size</span>     = <span class="text-num">24</span>;

<span class="text-kw">while</span> (<span class="text-var">$font</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getStringWidth</span>(<span class="text-var">$string</span>, <span class="text-var">$size</span>) &gt; <span class="text-var">$maxWidth</span> <span class="text-kw">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class="text-var">$size</span> &gt; <span class="text-num">1</span>) {
    <span class="text-var">$size</span><span class="text-kw">--</span>;
}
<span class="text-comment">// $size is 15, where the string measures 194.22 points wide</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="checking-what-is-available">Checking What Is Available<a class="anchor" href="#checking-what-is-available" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>isFontAvailable()</code> and its alias <code>hasFont()</code> both answer whether a name has been registered on the
document, and <code>getAvailableFonts()</code> lists every one that has:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Font</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>();
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFonts</span>([<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">HELVETICA</span>, <span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">TIMES_BOLD</span>]);

<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">isFontAvailable</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Helvetica&#039;</span>); <span class="text-comment">// true</span>
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">hasFont</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Helvetica&#039;</span>);         <span class="text-comment">// true, same check</span>
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">isFontAvailable</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;Arial&#039;</span>);     <span class="text-comment">// false — never registered</span>
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getAvailableFonts</span>();          <span class="text-comment">// [&#039;Helvetica&#039;, &#039;Times-Bold&#039;]</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Those three ask what the <em>document</em> has registered. <code>isStandard()</code>, on a <code>Font</code> object itself, asks a
different question — whether that particular font is one of the standard names rather than a file
loaded from disk:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Font</span>;

(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Font</span>(<span class="text-type">Font</span>::<span class="text-num">HELVETICA</span>))-&gt;<span class="text-fn">isStandard</span>(); <span class="text-comment">// true</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Combining the two answers what a document is actually carrying — every registered name alongside
whether it embeds anything:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addFont</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/fonts/DejaVuSans.ttf&#039;</span>);

<span class="text-kw">foreach</span> (<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getAvailableFonts</span>() <span class="text-kw">as</span> <span class="text-var">$name</span>) {
    <span class="text-var">$font</span> = <span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getFont</span>(<span class="text-var">$name</span>);
    <span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$name</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;: &#039;</span> . (<span class="text-var">$font</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">isStandard</span>() ? <span class="text-str">&#039;standard&#039;</span> : <span class="text-str">&#039;embedded&#039;</span>) . <span class="text-str">&quot;\n&quot;</span>;
}
<span class="text-comment">// Helvetica: standard</span>
<span class="text-comment">// Times-Bold: standard</span>
<span class="text-comment">// DejaVuSans: embedded</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

